<p>Upvoted, although for some reason the body horror didn't have the same impact as in the draft I read. More than made up for by the density of the rest of it - I particularly like how neatly 029 was woven in.</p>
<p>A few drafting points:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>These SCP-2833 instances were previously ambushed by GOC operatives, wherein an SCP-2833 instance was terminated as a result.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I didn't understand this sentence. Were the 2833 instances ambushed before the Foundation found them (and how did the Foundation know either that it was the GOC or that one of the instances died)? And &quot;wherein&quot; doesn't seem correct - &quot;whereby&quot; is closer (although wouldn't require &quot;as a result&quot; at the end of the sentence), but I think &quot;resulting in the death of an SCP-2833 instance&quot; is probably better.</p>
<ul>
<li>&quot;overran&quot; should be &quot;overrun&quot;</li>
<li>&quot;the &quot;Daughter of Shadow&quot; <span style="text-decoration: underline;">survive</span> the implantation ritual.&quot; should be &quot;survived&quot;.</li>
</ul>

